    <!-- Add insight / key takeaway directly related to activity / learner experience -->

     <insight>
        <title>Key Takeaway</title>
           <p>
             Angles are measured from the positive <m>x -</m> axis. It is also important to note that positive angles are measured in the counterclockwise(left-hand side) direction, 
             while negative angles are measured in the clockwise(right-hand side) direction.
          </p>
          <p>
            Whether a trigonometric value is positive or negative depends on the quadrant in which the angle lies .
            <hint>
                <p>
                    Kindly ensure that whenever you want to determine the quadrant in which an angle lies,begin from the positive <m>x -</m> axis and move(rotate) in the correct direction.
                </p>
            </hint>
            A better illustration of this is shown in the image below:
          </p>
          <p>
            <image source="path (no extension)">
                <shortdescription></shortdescription>
            </image>
          </p>
          <p>
             Remember that the primary ratios are:
          </p>
          <p>
            <ul>
                <li>
                    <p>
                        <m>\sin(\theta)= y</m> and <m>\cos(\theta)= x</m> where <m>(x,y)</m> is the point on the unit circle corresponding to the angle <m>\theta</m>.
                    </p>
                </li>
                <li>
                    <p>
                        <m>\tan(\theta)= \frac{y}{x}</m>
                    </p>
                </li>
            </ul>
          </p>
    </insight> 

